Z||000002||fyerstarter||03-28-2001||03:46 AM||||Suspension Techniques makes a set of 1.5 inch drop coils. They are cheaper than the Eibachs and slghtly lower but feature a linear spring rate rather than progressive. They can be found at JCWhitney, Discount Tire, Shox.com and probably anywhere else that sells ST Springs. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||03-28-2001||09:23 AM||||I got suspension techniques and put them on last week. it is dropped 1.5" and thats nice, it wasn't too terribly hard to do with 2 people.<BR>my only problem is, and i dont know if this is normal, but when im trying to turn real sharply, like in a parking lot, i hear this loud knock when the wheels are all the way turned. When I had the car aligned, they said everything else about the front end was good after they fixed a bad tie rod.<BR>Ah well, oh and it doesn't even ride that bad, except on really really crappy roads. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
